# datasets.list.example - which ZFS datasets the nightly backup covers.
# Real copy lives on the server: /mnt/SSDs/houseos/backup/datasets.list (not in git).
#
# One rule per line:  <action> <dataset>   # optional reason
#   include  back up this dataset and all its children
#   exclude  a child of an included dataset to leave out (caches, logs)
#   skip     deliberately not backed up - always write why
#
# Every dataset in the pool must be covered by a rule (directly or through a parent).
# The script warns about any that aren't, so new datasets can't go unprotected silently.

include  POOL/app-data
include  POOL/photos
exclude  POOL/app-data/someapp/cache       # rebuildable, changes constantly
skip     POOL/downloads                    # in-progress, re-downloadable